mage": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_012_thumb.jpg", "page": "12", "label": "12", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/12"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_013_thumb.jpg", "page": "13", "label": "13", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/13"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_014_thumb.jpg", "page": "14", "label": "14", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/14"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_015_thumb.jpg", "page": "15", "label": "15", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/15"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_016_thumb.jpg", "page": "16", "label": "16", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/16"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_017_thumb.jpg", "page": "17", "label": "17", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/17"}, {"image": "/430/430_ms4583_1_71_017-01_thumb.jpg", "page": "18", "label": "[18]", "href": "/paper-summary/letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839/18"}], "tableOfContents": [], "summary": {"uri": "letter-to-the-church-and-edward-partridge-20-march-1839", "series": "JSPPD", "urlTitleValue": "JSPPD6", "documentSeriesTitle": "Letter to the Church and Edward Partridge, 20 March 1839", "editorialPageNumber": "4", "isPageNumberPresent": true, "searchUrl": "/published/jsp/searchable/papers/21225849/21225849-0004.xml", "clearText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> and thine ear be penetrated with their cyes [cries] yea o Lord how long shall they suffer these rongs and unlawfull oppressions before thine hart shall be softened towards them and thy bowels be moved with compassion to-words them. O Lord God almity maker of heaven earth and seas and of all things that in them is<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"1929539823277054146\"><a href=\"#1929539823277054146\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans15\"><span id=\"documenttrans15\">15</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Exodus 20:11.</p><hr></div></div></aside> and who controleth and subjecteth the devil and the dark and benighted dominion of shayole. Streach forth thy hand let thine eye pierce let thy pavilion be taken up let thy hiding place no longer be covered<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"14352689073495447585\"><a href=\"#14352689073495447585\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans16\"><span id=\"documenttrans16\">16</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 16–17 December 1833 [D&amp;C\n101]\">Revelation, 16–17 Dec. 1833</a> [D&amp;C 101:89].</p><hr></div></div></aside> let thine ear be inclined<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"4038166292749551091\"><a href=\"#4038166292749551091\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans17\"><span id=\"documenttrans17\">17</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Psalm 102:2.</p><hr></div></div></aside> let thine hart be softened and thy bowels moved with compassion toward us let thine anger be kindle against our enemies and in the fury of thine hart with thy sword avenge us of our rongs remember thy suffering saint oh our God and thy servants will rejoyce in thy name for ever.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"7699430926050857222\"><a href=\"#7699430926050857222\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans18\"><span id=\"documenttrans18\">18</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Psalm 89:16.</p><hr></div></div></aside> Dearly and beloved Brethren we see that peralas [perilous] times have come as was testified of<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"15377487979631025972\"><a href=\"#15377487979631025972\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans19\"><span id=\"documenttrans19\">19</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See 2 Timothy 3:1.</p><hr></div></div></aside> we may look then with most purfect asshurance for the roling in of all those things that have been written and with more confidence than ever before lift up our eyes to the luminary of day and say in our harts soon thou wilt vail thy blushing face he that said let there be light, and there was light<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"10507109234520344133\"><a href=\"#10507109234520344133\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans20\"><span id=\"documenttrans20\">20</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Genesis 1:3.</p><hr></div></div></aside> hath spoken this word, and again thou moon thou dimmer light thou luminary of night shall turn to blood<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"16688570176198245138\"><a href=\"#16688570176198245138\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans21\"><span id=\"documenttrans21\">21</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Joel 2:31; Revelation 6:12; and <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-september-1830-a-dc-29\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-september-1830-a-dc-29\" poptitle=\"Revelation, September 1830–A [D&amp;C\n29]\">Revelation, Sept. 1830–A</a> [D&amp;C 29:14].</p><hr></div></div></aside> we see that evry thing is fulfilling and the time shall soon come when the son of man shall [p. 4]</div></body></html>", "expandedText": "<html><head></head><body><div class=\"indent continuation wasptag\"> and thine ear be penetrated with their cyes [cries] <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>yea o Lord how long shall they suffer these rongs <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>and unlawfull oppressions before thine hart shall <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>be softened towards them and thy bowels be <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>moved with compassion to-words them. O Lord <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>God almity maker of heaven earth and seas <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>and of all things that in them is<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"14926967095029264633\"><a href=\"#14926967095029264633\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans15\"><span id=\"documenttrans15\">15</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Exodus 20:11.</p><hr></div></div></aside> and who controleth <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>and subjecteth the devil and the dark and benig[h<span class=\"line-break hyphenate\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>]ted dominion of shayole. Streach forth thy hand <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>let thine eye pierce let thy pavilion be taken <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>up let thy hiding place no longer be covered<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"7146077138633199902\"><a href=\"#7146077138633199902\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans16\"><span id=\"documenttrans16\">16</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See <a href=\"/paper-summary/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" class=\"referenceInPop\" pop=\"/ajax/papers/tooltip/revelation-16-17-december-1833-dc-101\" poptitle=\"Revelation, 16–17 December 1833 [D&amp;C\n101]\">Revelation, 16–17 Dec. 1833</a> [D&amp;C 101:89].</p><hr></div></div></aside> <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>let thine ear be inclined<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"1319967069152706288\"><a href=\"#1319967069152706288\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans17\"><span id=\"documenttrans17\">17</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Psalm 102:2.</p><hr></div></div></aside> let thine hart be softened <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>and thy bowels moved with compassion toward <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>us let thine anger be kindle against our enemi[e]s <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>and in the fury of thine hart with thy sword <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>avenge us of our rongs remember thy suffering <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>saint oh our God and thy servants will rejoyce <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>in thy name for ever.<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"7791908053140284571\"><a href=\"#7791908053140284571\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans18\"><span id=\"documenttrans18\">18</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Psalm 89:16.</p><hr></div></div></aside> Dearly and beloved Brethren <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>we see that peralas [perilous] times have come as was <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>testified of<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"17449582334973067909\"><a href=\"#17449582334973067909\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans19\"><span id=\"documenttrans19\">19</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See 2 Timothy 3:1.</p><hr></div></div></aside> we may look then with most <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>purfect asshurance for the roling in of all those <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>things that have been written and with more <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>confidence than ever before lift up our eyes <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>to the luminary of day and say in our harts <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>soon thou wilt vail thy blushing face he that <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>said let there be light, and there was light<aside class=\"popup-wrapper\" id=\"14085174052019580939\"><a href=\"#14085174052019580939\" class=\"editorial-note-static staticPopup\" title=\"Note\" name=\"trans20\"><span id=\"documenttrans20\">20</span></a><div class=\"popup-content\"><div class=\"note-data editorial-footnote\" isnote=\"Y\"><p class=\"bottom_0\">See Genesis 1:3.</p><hr></div></div></aside> hath <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>spoken this word, and again thou moon thou <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"></span>dimmer light thou luminary of night shall <span class=\"deleted\">trurn</span> &lt;​turn​&gt; <span class=\"line-break\" xmlns=